{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 40,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The biggest issue\nin 20 years will be population collapse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4200,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we're looking at the Chinese\nrunning out of people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7080,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Within ten years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8600,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The population collapse in developed\ncountries is precipitous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13600,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A demographic earthquake\nis going to destroy our economies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17400,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fewer workers, fewer ideas, higher taxes\nto fund more pensioners, slower growth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22120,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By now, you've probably heard all the doom\nand gloom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24720,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arguments,\nperhaps even on this very channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27720,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what if we wait?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29520,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What if I was wrong?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31440,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What if the historical evidence\nactually tells us that collapsing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34560,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "birthrates, paradoxically,\nare good for the economy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39000,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because they force companies to innovate?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42240,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's exactly the premise of a new paper\nby Nobel Prize winning economist Darren"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46920,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Asamoah and coauthors\nthat has been going econo viral on X."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53160,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this paper,\nhe studies some of the biggest fertility"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56080,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collapses of all time\nChina, Japan and South Korea."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59840,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they found that these coincided\nwith growth miracles, not disasters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, it turns out that countries\nwith the lowest fertility rates back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69840,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1950 turned out to grow faster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72920,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the next 70 years than countries\nthat still had lots of babies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77000,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, if we look at history,\nit seems like collapsing birthrates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81600,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are not that bad\nand may even be good for the economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85240,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But does that encouraging evidence\nactually apply"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to our coming demographic doom story?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91080,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before we can find out,\nlet's quickly review"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93960,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the standard story\nthe global economy faces demographic doom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98440,
    "dDurationMs": 360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As I see it, there are essentially\ntwo parts to this story"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102000,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about why a rapidly aging society\nis bad news for the economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106680,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Far fewer workers will have to support\na lot of pensioners."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The economy GDP is simply a measure\nof all goods and services produced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116640,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you rapidly reduce\nthe number of people who make stuff versus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120480,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those that are retired,\nand of course you should expect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123720,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economic growth to slow down rapidly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126800,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes. Slow down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128320,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the thing is,\neconomic growth is not just hours worked."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132440,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's also how productively\nthese hours are used."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135720,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So far, even a rapidly aging economy\nlike Japan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139120,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been able to grow\nby getting more productive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141840,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, sadly, the second\npart of the doom and gloom story"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145600,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "predicts that as fewer babies are born,\nworkers will be less productive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149640,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because there will be less innovation\nfor two reasons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reason number one\nyoung workers are uniquely innovative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fewer babies today mean fewer\nentrepreneurs and inventors tomorrow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, beyond the fact\nthat older workers tend to start fewer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164280,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high growth startups, aging workforces\ncreate massive bottlenecks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170040,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is when senior employees hold onto\nkey positions for longer and longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174840,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They prevent younger talent\nfrom acquiring the management"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178000,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and business skills needed to succeed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181240,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, economists\nlike doctor Fatih Garan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184720,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "argue\nthat roughly half of the decline in U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188320,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "startup activity\nsince the 1980s can be explained"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192160,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "purely by fewer young Americans\nentering the workforce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195640,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second,\nwhen a population is growing rapidly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198320,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is a big prize\nfor those who innovate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201360,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Put yourself in the shoes\nof an ambitious software entrepreneur."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204240,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Competing with established giants requires\nimmense upfront investments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210080,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the population is growing,\nso does your future customer base,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214440,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making it worth\nthe risk to build new products."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217280,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in a country facing\ndemographic decline, where the pool"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220520,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of potential business\nclients shrinks year after year,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the price for innovation might simply\nnot be big enough anymore to justify"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228920,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spending so many years on researching\nand trying potential new products."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233320,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in summary,\nthe standard narrative is twofold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236400,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One. Fewer babies means fewer\nworkers, means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239120,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less supply of goods and services\nsimple to fewer young people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a falling population\nmeans less innovation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246240,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And together, these two trends\nspell certain doom for the economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250680,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that is just a theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252920,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a theory\nmust always answer to evidence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256320,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And according to some Moghalu\nand his coauthors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the evidence does not support this story\nat all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261680,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, aging"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will reduce the number of workers,\nbut rather than becoming less innovative,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266960,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they believe a reduced workforce will make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269760,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economies more innovative, not less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And crucially,\nthis positive effect will be stronger"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276000,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the negative effect\nof having fewer workers, at least."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This happened\nclearly when people least expected it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283600,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "during a time of war\nor war, and its unexpected blessings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289440,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's 1809 and Britain is at war\nwith France for control of the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293920,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Royal Navy soon runs short of sailors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297240,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so every captain suddenly\nhas to find his own crew however he can,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301440,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looking for volunteers,\ntaking men of passing merchant ships and,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crucially, recruiting many unexperienced\nfarmers and workers off the coast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, the Navy recruited\nmostly farm men from coastal regions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315400,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course close to the deep waters\nwhere the biggest warships could anchor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320120,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, these regions last prime\nworking age males to fight the French,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324720,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this caused, of course,\nlabor shortages and as a consequence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328240,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those that stayed behind could, in theory\nask a higher wage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As economists Joachim von\nand his colleagues show, that is exactly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336280,
    "dDurationMs": 760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337040,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The higher the recruitment in an area,\nthe higher the wage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340920,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Agricultural servants\non annual contracts and day laborers got."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345680,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, that makes sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346880,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This turned out to be a crucial factor\nbehind the mechanization of British farms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353080,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a shift that many point out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the peak starter\nfor the Industrial Revolution in Britain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358600,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Already back in the 1780s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360840,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Andrew Maxwell had built\nthe first threshing machine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it was expensive\nand somewhat unreliable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368400,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for two decades it had only made sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in northern England,\nwhere wages were already fairly high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374160,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In southern England, it was cheaper\nto hire a man to do the work instead."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378480,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, as labor became\nmore expensive due to war, recruitment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382920,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "machines essentially became cheaper\ncompared to labor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387160,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So machines, of course, ended up\nshowing up exactly in places"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that had an higher number of men recruited\nto fight in the war against France."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396840,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hence, for these regions, paradoxically,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399560,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "losing young workers\nwas the opposite of a catastrophe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402880,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead,\nit became an incentive to innovate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply\nbecause labor was getting too expensive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is what the standard doom story\nmisses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More pessimistic economists\nlike Professor Charles Goodhart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do stress that fewer workers will likely\ncause wages to rise, causing inflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421560,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's a bad thing,\nbut they typically do not stress so much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425880,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that this could be a major boost\nto innovation, because higher wages"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429840,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "force firms to innovate,\nwhich ultimately makes remaining workers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434040,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more productive,\ncausing the economy to grow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this happened more than 200 years ago,\nand it's just a single case study."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442560,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, as a moghalu and his coauthors\npresent way more evidence in the paper"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specifically on how the past 70 years\nof falling birth rates affected economies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452960,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To answer this question, Asim\nMoghalu and his coauthors compared"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456440,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "70 years of birth rate and GDP data across\nmore than a hundred countries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462480,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a lot of data. Very impressive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465000,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you can see here,\ntheir findings are clear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467800,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lower birth rates in 1950\ncorrelate with higher GDP growth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472720,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, this in itself\ndoes not prove the innovation story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476560,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, the researchers dug deeper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479760,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After tracking millions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480840,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of battered records worldwide,\nthey found a striking pattern."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485040,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you can see here in these graphs,\nthe higher the birth rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488080,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1950, the fewer patents were filed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492000,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by implication, countries with fewer\nbirth rates actually innovate more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498280,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which again\ncontradicts the standard story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500880,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And crucially,\nthese inventions did not just sit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503880,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on shelves\ncollecting dust in patent offices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They transformed real world economies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510560,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reading our graph again,\nwe see that countries with more births"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514880,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1950s went on to export significantly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518120,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fewer high tech products in the decades\nthat followed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521480,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, low birth countries\nexported more high tech products."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527640,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were more innovative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529680,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This provides an additional layer to the\neconomic miracles of both dependent China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533640,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both nations started out exporting cheap,\nsimple goods to Western markets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537840,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and quickly moved up the ladder\ninto advanced,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sophisticated industries like robotics,\nelectronics and high tech manufacturing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545520,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As their birth rate collapsed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547760,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, while many factors drove this\ntransition from industrial policy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551720,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to global trade demand,\nthe things that we often discuss"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554040,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the channel\nthe urgent need to replace a shrinking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557080,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "younger generation of workers\nwas potentially an underrated factor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562440,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So history\nso far contradicts actually the main doom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565560,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and gloom\nnarrative of demographic decline."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fewer workers do not automatically mean\nless innovation, on the contrary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Countries facing labor scarcity\nhave often adapted technology"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577040,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to compensate for missing heads,\nmaking the average worker"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580320,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "significantly more productive\nin the process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does this mean that the standard\npessimistic story is entirely wrong,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587400,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that falling fertility\nrates will simply make us all richer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591840,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sadly, no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592680,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because\nthis time may actually be different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596640,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, the present\ndoes not have to be like the past."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in this case,\nI think there are two main weaknesses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the new positive story presented\nby Professor Acemoglu and his coauthors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608080,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, fertility rates in the 1950s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610400,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were very different to our current rates\nthat are ultra low."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614680,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1950,\nthe country with the lowest fertility rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on Earth was Austria,\nand it was still at 2.0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622040,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's very close to the replacement level\nneeded to hold the population steady."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626520,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, South Korea is at 0.8."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629280,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you hold that for a generation,\nthe next generation will be 38%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633200,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "smaller than last."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634560,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this isn't just a projection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636400,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's already happening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637720,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Korea was delivering around 650,000 babies\na year at the start of the 1990s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642920,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but last year it was closer to 230,000."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646200,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those 1980s and 1990s\nbabies are the engineers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650040,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "designing chips at Samsung right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652800,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the classrooms behind\nthem are two thirds empty."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656760,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure, some of those remaining students\nwill still grow up to become"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660720,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brilliant engineers\nand creative inventors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663600,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's hard to believe that such\na massive collapse in the talent pool,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something we have not seen before,\nwill not lead to less innovation overall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672560,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the scary math of ultra\nlow fertility."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675360,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It gets worse over\ntime, driving population decline"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678320,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "faster\nthan anything we've seen in human history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682600,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We simply did not have\nthis dynamic back in 1950, when virtually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686080,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every country on earth was sitting\nwell above the replacement level."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690680,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the second weakness in a similar\nstory is that he just looks at falling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694360,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "birth rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695440,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, that is a trend\nthat has been happening for a long time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699040,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, what I'm worried about\nis actually the ratio"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701960,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of pensioners compared to active workers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705360,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More specifically, what I'm worried about\nis the changing dependency ratio."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709240,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, those who do not work, that\ndepend on those who work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712720,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see,\nwhile you may say how strange that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "falling birth rates\ncoincided with an economic miracle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719040,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would instead\nlook at the dependency ratio of both kids"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723240,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and old people in the 1950s,\nall the way up to the 20 tens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The dependency ratio\nwas actually falling fast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in China and Korea,\nbut now it's starting to rise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734240,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is a very different trend."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736440,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some demographic researchers\ncall the times of falling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dependency ratios a positive demographic\ndividend for a reason."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744360,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Having two young kids myself,\nI can definitely tell you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I became far less willing\nto take massive entrepreneurial risks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751680,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since I became a dad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753000,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the fact that falling birth rates,\na period of demographic dividend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757160,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coincided with a productivity boom\ndoes not surprise me at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761400,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now,\nwith more elderly people to take care of,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764680,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the world is heading into a period\nof reverse demographic dividend today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769080,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is fundamentally different\nthan the period"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771520,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a small group studied in his paper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773560,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in conclusion,\nwhere I and other economists wrong about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778240,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "warning for the economic consequences,\nthe doom story of more and more pensioners"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783080,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with fewer workers to depend on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786000,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps, but\nI was not fully convinced by this paper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791000,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that the simple fact\nthat so many people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793440,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stop working while the remaining workers\nhave to pay for their pensions presents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797400,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a huge, never\nbefore seen risk to the global economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802360,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the paper we discuss today\ndid make me more hopeful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807600,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that rather than gray economies becoming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less innovative, rising workers shortages"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813680,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could actually force them\nto become more innovative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just like what happened in southern\nEngland during the war with France,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821360,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which I surely would have expected\nwould have been negative for the economy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825120,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the way I see it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826160,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each of these three effects\ncan be true at the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830000,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The question that really matters is\nwhich effects will be stronger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834760,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sadly, historical economic research\ncannot yet answer that question"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839160,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because a new wave\nand falling population levels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843360,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is simply something\nthat we have never seen before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848080,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's my take."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849560,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What do you think?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850600,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Will the negative effects\nof falling workers to pensioners"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and eventually falling population levels"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858320,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be stronger than the potential effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861880,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of increased innovation\nafter labor costs are pushed higher,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because companies will have to innovate\nso much faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869400,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me know in the comments below\nand if you want to learn more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872840,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about the economic effects\nof demographic decline,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875240,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I highly recommend that you check out\nthe following three articles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879520,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from our advertising sponsor,\nThe Economist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883160,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Start with this piece on why panics over\nbirth rates are often overblown,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887640,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which I think provides\na very balanced treatment of the optimists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891160,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pessimist cases\naround demographic decline."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, for what happens when governments\ntry to engineer or change fertility"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899160,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "directly, read this analysis on the long\nshadow of China's one child policy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904240,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, if you want to see\nwhether the world's population growth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906920,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will actually be decided."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908800,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This article on Nigeria\nis absolutely fascinating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912480,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Women in the South have half\nas many children as women in the North."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916520,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the reasons will give you a couple\nof key insights about the population"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920720,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "growth\nthat will change the world that in Africa."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924120,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As these examples show,\nThe Economist delivers insights"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927240,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that will help you see the bigger picture\nand think for yourself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930720,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is why I almost always rely\non their analysis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933560,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for my research, and it's why\nI highly recommend that you subscribe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936800,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
